Idea:
You are given a bunch of "monsters", each described by a single integer. This integer acts as the health as well as 
strength of the monster. You have the ability to make two monsters fight each other. If two monsters fight, first monster1 hits monster2
which results in monster2 losing monster1 points. After that if monster2 has > 0 points left, the roles switch, i.e. the monsters
keep hitting each other until one of them is dead. 

Example: A monster with strength 7 fights a monster with strength 11:
m1  m2
7   11
7   4
3   4
3   1
2   1
2   0

The goal is to find two monsters, s.t. after the fight one monster has 0 strength and the other one 1 strength left.

Solution:
In the end we want the monsters to have strengths 0 and 1. This means that before the last hit, their strengths must have been 1 and 1.
Before that they must have been 1 and 2, before that 3 and 2. This gives the Fibonacci-sequence.
=> Put all numbers into a set, iterate the Fibonacci sequence up to the max. in the set and check if two consecutive Fibonacci numbers
are in the set. The case where >= 2 monsters of strength 1 are given needs to be handled separately.

Constraints:
1 <= number of monsters <= 10^5
1 <= strength of monster <= 10^8

Difficulty:
Easy
I expect > 90% to solve this problem.
 